    {
      "id": "49i25gt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Difference Between Plant Cell and Animal Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mitochondria are frequently asked in exams as the 'Powerhouse of the Cell' due to ATP production.",
        "Lysosomes are commonly termed 'Suicidal Bags' because of their hydrolytic digestive enzymes.",
        "Ribosomes are the non-membrane-bound organelles responsible for protein synthesis in both prokaryotes and eukaryotes.",
        "Plant cell walls are made of cellulose, whereas fungal cell walls are made of chitin."
      ],
      "id": "5fmoijg"
    },
